#!/usr/bin/env bash
set +e
cat > /tmp/index.html <<'EOF'
<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>How to Build a Better Multi-Platform Social Media Growth Framework</title><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"></head><body><main style="max-width:900px;margin:40px auto;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.75;padding:0 20px"><h1>How to Build a Better Multi-Platform Social Media Growth Framework</h1><p>Social media growth becomes more useful when it is connected to a measurable business objective. The strongest campaigns combine audience research, useful content, profile optimization, analytics, conversion planning, and carefully selected promotional support. Businesses comparing external providers can include <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/">SMM Fans Faster</a> in a broader evaluation of platform coverage, delivery conditions, support, order limits, refill policies, and campaign suitability.</p><h2>Start with clear campaign objectives</h2><p>Awareness, engagement, traffic, and sales campaigns require different metrics. Awareness may focus on reach and video views. Engagement may prioritize watch time, comments, saves, shares, and return viewers. Conversion should connect social activity with profile visits, website clicks, inquiries, leads, bookings, purchases, and revenue. Recording a baseline before scaling makes later analysis more accurate.</p><h2>Create repeatable content pillars</h2><p>Educational posts, demonstrations, comparisons, customer stories, industry insights, FAQs, and offers can become repeatable content pillars. The same core topic can be presented with different hooks, formats, examples, and calls to action. This gives the marketing team enough consistency to identify patterns without making the account feel repetitive.</p><h2>Use TikTok for rapid creative testing</h2><p>TikTok provides fast feedback on hooks, pacing, editing, and topic selection. Marketers researching additional growth support can review information about <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-followers">TikTok followers</a> and <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/tiktok-views">TikTok views, followers, and likes</a>. These signals are most useful when considered together with retention, completion rate, comments, shares, saves, and profile visits.</p><p>It can also help to review information about the <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/numberoftiktokfollowers">number of TikTok followers</a>. Milestones may contribute to social proof, but they should not replace content quality or audience relevance.</p><h2>Improve Instagram conversion after discovery</h2><p>Instagram combines discovery, education, community, and conversion. Reels can attract new users, carousels can explain detailed topics, Stories can maintain regular contact, and highlights can organize important information. Marketers can review this guide to an <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/blog/instagram-followers-website">Instagram followers website</a> while comparing available growth options.</p><p>It is also useful to understand whether <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/ar/blog/doesincreasingyourfollowersaffecttheinstagramalgorithmfindoutnow">increasing followers affects the Instagram algorithm</a> and whether <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/ar/blog/doesbuyinginstagramfollowersaffectengagement">buying Instagram followers affects engagement</a>. Healthy account performance should include saves, shares, comments, profile visits, clicks, messages, and conversions.</p><h2>Measure the full funnel</h2><p>A strong reporting framework separates awareness, engagement, conversion, and revenue. Strong reach with weak profile activity can indicate low relevance. Strong profile visits with weak clicks may suggest that the bio or call to action needs work. Strong traffic with poor conversion can point to a landing-page, offer, pricing, or checkout problem.</p><h2>Use automation carefully</h2><p>Agencies and resellers managing multiple accounts can review the public <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/api">SMM API documentation</a> and the <a href="https://smmfansfaster.com/smm-api-integration">SMM API integration</a> page. Automation can reduce repetitive tasks, but human review should remain part of target selection, quantity checks, campaign objectives, and quality control.</p><h2>Final thoughts</h2><p>Sustainable growth comes from the interaction between audience understanding, strong creative work, profile optimization, analytics, promotion, and conversion. The best campaigns use external promotional services as one measurable component of a broader strategy rather than treating them as a replacement for content or real audience engagement.</p></main></body></html>
EOF
size=$(wc -c < /tmp/index.html | tr -d ' ')
sha=$(sha256sum /tmp/index.html | awk '{print $1}')
payload=$(jq -n --arg sha "$sha" --argjson size "$size" '{files:[{path:"index.html",size:$size,contentType:"text/html",sha256:$sha}]}')
create=$(curl -sS -X POST 'https://api.xdr.no/api/v1/publish' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$payload")
url=$(echo "$create" | jq -r '.url // empty')
put=$(echo "$create" | jq -r '.uploads[0].putUrl // empty')
final=$(echo "$create" | jq -r '.finalize // empty')
if [ -n "$put" ]; then curl -sS -X PUT "$put" -H 'Content-Type: text/html' --data-binary @/tmp/index.html >/dev/null; fi
if [ -n "$final" ]; then curl -sS -X POST "$final" >/dev/null; fi
echo "RESULT_URL=$url"
